{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head b6a7ba3220018d470dc918cc4fdc73f4d01eb958, tree cab6ae4c05a19ec3aed2dd6883ce42d6118d4dc3, on builder/xd1-owner-20261116, all 4 artifacts, for request de00a2f5 under my promise bacb2db0. This verdict names the one implementation: XD-1 step 1b (request 2ccdefb0, promise 34fee568, report dd649fd6, the XD-1 note, primary). `gs review --prepare` resolved that binding at this head, with the request closing on the sealed receipt. Main d6c863bb is the base, and two commits change four paths.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- The setup file. A `beforeEach` maps each test context's `signal` to the test's file and full name, in a WeakMap that is global across the isolate. The guard looks up the aborted controller's `signal`. So a timer of test A that fires while test B runs names A, and an unregistered controller names `(no owner)`. With `SWALLOW_CROSSING = false`, behaviour is unchanged: the guard prints one line and rethrows.\n- The guard. `guardAbort` now passes the controller to `report`. The rest is unchanged.\n- The control. The new Node case registers two controllers, aborts A's controller, and gets one line that names A.\n- The note. It now says that a line shows a fired timer that workerd refused to abort, not a test past its limit. It records both owners in `archive-driver.test.ts` (786 ms and 736 ms, both passed), the probe, and the untested cause. It also says that step 3 as written fails nothing for a stale timer.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. The 4 artifacts name the head, no path repeats, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only d6c863bb b6a7ba32`.\n- The gate, END 6ef25924. `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-16-xd1-owner-gate/gate.log` names head 7c4f4d6a and tree ff9fee62 with 0 changed files. Pins passed in 19.1 s. Plain 4957 with 1 skipped and Native 1173 with 2 skipped passed, with 2 crossings, and the last line is \"gate passed\". From 7c4f4d6a to this head, only the note changes. A notes-only change needs no new gate.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 2 checked, 0 flagged. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The owner comes from the test's own context, which Vitest aborts. It does not come from a global \"current test\", which is wrong by construction when a timer fires late.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The change touches only test support and a Node test.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nTwo points for the note, not blocking:\n\n1. The first paragraph still says that a test past its limit \"does not fail. It keeps running and can pass.\" No run has shown such a test yet: every line so far is a stale timer of a passed test. State that the lost rejection is possible by source, and that the observed lines are all stale timers.\n2. A `beforeAll` or `afterAll` hook has no test context, so its timer reports `(no owner)`. Say so under \"Read the line\", so that a reader does not read `(no owner)` as a fault of the guard.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner rules on steps 2 and 3 and decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:dd649fd6f1a4032ddc07aa70885de0f9387694c0","binding":"assigned","head":"b6a7ba3220018d470dc918cc4fdc73f4d01eb958","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bacb2db036ecfbf93b379a59b8789c0209ad1241\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:34fee5686589f1904b92fa46eff6a1a7b850a192\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bacb2db036ecfbf93b379a59b8789c0209ad1241","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}